<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2500" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ancŏra</span></b> , ae (not <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anchŏra</span></b> ), f.
		v. ango, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγκῦρα</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>an anchor.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I. A..</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ancora fundabat naves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
					6, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jacere,</span>”
				<i>to cast anchor</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 4, 28</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mittere,</span>”
				<i>to let go</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Act. 27, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">extendere,</span>”
				<i>to put out</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">ib. ib. 27, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naves deligare ad ancoras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 4, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navem tenere in ancoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Them. 8, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consistere ad ancoram,</span>”
				<i>to lie at anchor</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 3, 102</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naves in ancoris constiterunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 28</span></i>
			 et saep.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solvere,</span>”
				<i>to weigh anchor</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 1, 13</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tollere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 1, 31</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act. 27, 40</span></i>; also, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in gen.,</span>”
				<i>to depart</i>, <i>go away</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 17, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vellere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecidere,</span>”
				<i>to cut the cables</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Verr. 2, 5, 34 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, as a symbol of security, <i>refuge</i>, <i>hope</i>, <i>support</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ancora jam nostram non tenet ulla ratem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 5, 2, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ultima fessis ancora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. 7,
					24</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spem, quam sicut ancoram habemus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Heb. 6, 10</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>an iron in the form
				of an anchor</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 40,
		5</span></i>.</div>
